Typically “,”; anything is fine as long as it doesn’t appear within the actual data.

In Europe where “,” is often used in numbers (like “0,758” where Americans generally write  “0.758”) sometimes sep=“.”. There’s an additional argument, dec, for the character used as the decimal point, so for example dec=“,”.

karl

